## 9. Describe a complex problem you solved

→ In my LabFlow project, we faced duplicate and out-of-order Kafka events and concurrent updates to laboratory results.

→ Duplicate events could cause repeated processing, while concurrent updates could overwrite newer results.

→ I used idempotent processing, result versioning, the Transactional Outbox pattern, and optimistic locking to improve reliability and consistency.

→ I also worked on database performance and production issues such as Kafka consumer lag and notification failures.

